DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T210000
SUMMARY:Halloween in Evil Bloody York - (2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nMuddy York\, T
 oronto after 1834 was a **not so innocent** little town as one might think
 .\n\nIt had its share of death and destruction. arson\, murder\, plenty of
  murder\, and ghost sightings after these events. Wild stories to tell chi
 ldren around the camp fire. But these stories are true. Join me on a walk 
 around old Toronto\, and prepare for the Halloween season just ahead.\n\nH
 ave you heard about the Mad Dog of Jarvis street? Or what happened in the 
 old York Town Hall on a day when William Lyon was about to pull the curtai
 n down on the Family Compact\, you could say it got very sticky\, very qui
 ckly.\n\nAnd after this you could say that people were hooked on all the s
 tories. You could also say that people got hung up on William. Ok enough f
 un talk\, let's go exploring. A walking tour into the dark heart and secre
 ts of the Toronto we all love so much.\n\nStories that will make your Hall
 oween! And chill your blood. Sounds like a plan!\n\nLet's explore stories 
 of Toronto's bloodiest side!\n\nThis walking tour is for all levels and wa
 lkers. This tour is for children over the age of 12!\n\nThe tour begins on
  the steps of the Yorkville Library on Yorkville Avenue just west of Yonge
  Street. The tour ends at King Street East\, and Church Street.\n\nAnd jus
 t look for me. I'll be there\, or at least my spirit will be.......\n\nThi
 s tour has a ticket price of $15.00. Please **book early** as this tour fi
 lls up pretty quick.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket
  amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693
 148/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260924T123912Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T123912Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_316693116@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261017T041428Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T203000
SUMMARY:Ghosts of West Toronto - Halloween Event 2026
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nHalloween is th
 e best time to take in the ghosts that haunt our minds and our city. The c
 ity is not quite asleep yet and things roam. They cross our paths with the
  stories we tell. At the core of this tour\, two brutal stories that have 
 impacted Toronto\, are explored\, but have a ghostly following. You could 
 say this tour explores the old stories that stir the blood\, even after 15
 0 years.\n\nToronto is not a squeaky clean polished town\, it has plenty t
 o chill the blood. Stories of horror and crime and things that go bump in 
 the night abound.\n\nFrom the true horror of the Mercer Reformatory to the
  Central Prison in Liberty Village\, and the ghosts of the exhibition grou
 nds\, things that should be left alone will be dug up.\n\nMany other unexp
 lained happenings will be talked about\, this tour will haunt\, or at leas
 t you hope so! Well let's get through this one alive.\n\nThis walking tour
  is for all levels and walkers. The tour begins at the TTC Exhibition Stre
 etcar loop at the corner of Dufferin Street\, and Springhurst Avenue in Pa
 rkdale.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\nHope to s
 ee you there. And at the end of the tour hopefully you are still around. W
 ell maybe.....\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price
  when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the followin
 g email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693
 116/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260924T123506Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T123506Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_316693182@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261017T041428Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T210000
SUMMARY:Toronto Ghosts! A Halloween Event hosted by Jack the Ripper (RETUR
 N FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the tic
 ket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to th
 e following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\n**This tour 
 is hosted by the most evil creature that ever walked the earth\, Jack the 
 Ripper. This is his event so tread lightly if you know what is good for yo
 u. One day only\, one event! Need I say more!**\n\nHaunted Toronto. Indeed
 . Scary stories of old York. Bloody York. Murder and mayhem.\n\nAnd at thi
 s time of year when the chill cools the blood\, stories of the truly bruta
 l come out. And this walk is like no other.\n\nTales of hauntings from the
  U of T\, Hospital Row\, and the Financial District make this a spooky eve
 nt for all. Come and enjoy the walk\, if you survive that is!\n\nThis walk
 ing tour is for all fitness levels and skills. Please dress for the weathe
 r. This Halloween walking tour begins at the Queen's Park SUBWAY Station a
 t the southwest corner of University Avenue and College Street in front of
  the **Tim Horton's Cafe.**\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per 
 person.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when 
 booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following emai
 l at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693
 182/
